@page "/terms"
@inherits Live
<div class="panel" style="max-width:760px">
    <h2>Terms: arbitration</h2>
    <p>OpenTube is run by the people who use it; there is no company behind a transaction. By using it you agree to the following.</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Any dispute about a transaction made through OpenTube (a sale, an auction, a payment held in escrow) is resolved through the network’s own arbitration: the arbitration body named on the listing, and on appeal the levels above it. It is not a public court.</li>
        <li>Filings, case dockets and orders are public records on the network. Don’t file anything you need to keep private.</li>
        <li>A ruling decides how coins held in escrow are split. When that body’s appeal window passes, or the highest level has ruled, the ruling is final as far as the network is concerned.</li>
        <li>Goods, services and payments outside the network are between the parties; the arbitrators’ rulings and records are what the network provides.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="sub">This is a plain description of how the system works, not legal advice. Whether it binds you outside the network depends on where you live.</p>
    @if (S.Ready) { <button class="primary" disabled="@agreed" @onclick="Agree">@(agreed ? "Agreed ✓" : "I agree")</button> }
</div>
@code {
    bool agreed;
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() { base.OnInitialized(); if (S.Ready) agreed = await S.Social.Pref("termsAgreed") != null; }
    async Task Agree() { await S.Social.SetPref("termsAgreed", DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToString("o")); agreed = true; TermsBanner.Agreed?.Invoke(); }
}
